  "skip_compile_files": [
    // gsound's *sound-handles* (L383) and *sound-bank-reload-names* (L356) statics
    // emit as bare label refs; goal_src lands compilable hand-carries and the
    // decomp-vs-REF diff still gates all the code
    "gsound",
    // gsound-h's ambient-sound new (m0) fails on srl/pcpyud inline asm and emits
    // only the error comment block; goal_src lands the hand-carried method and the
    // decomp-vs-REF diff still gates the types and the other methods
    "gsound-h",
    // both statics now decompile clean (label_types.jsonc sizes L123 and the
    // apply()-abort fix in insert_static_refs stopped it from suppressing L122
    // right after); the remaining blocker is get-destruct-perm's raw (&-> ...) cast
    // to a symbol's value slot, which goalc types as (pointer object) without the
    // hand-cast goal_src carries; the decomp-vs-REF diff still gates the code
    "net-simple-destruct",
    "types-h", // weird array of types.
    // "hfrag-h", // weird duplicate type
    // the REFs record the parked VU0/scratchpad decompression family (joint) and the
    // raw-op parked methods (process-drawable) which do not compile; goal_src lands
    // the real bodies and the decomp-vs-REF diff still gates both
    "joint",
    "process-drawable",
    // "subdivide",
    "shadow-cpu-h",
    // jak3 parity: foreground-draw/-ripple carry undecompilable VU0 asm and
    // foreground-emerc never converts, so the whole file skips goalc in the
    // offline set (jak3's config does the same); the decomp-vs-REF diff still runs
    "foreground",
    // the retail static at L27 now decompiles clean (label_types.jsonc sizes it), but
    // codegen still fails: the decompiler emits two internal-named (method inspect
    // attackable-hash) definitions and goalc refuses the duplicate; goal_src hand-
    // authors the type and the decomp-vs-REF diff still gates the code
    "attackable-hash",
    // the REF records the parked gui-control/spooler/external-art surface, which
    // still carries CFG and type-prop errors; goal_src lands the art slice and
    // the decomp-vs-REF diff still gates the whole object
    "loader",
    // credits-obs: *credits-chars* is a raw <static-data L157> blob, a top-level
    // define the compiler tokenizes as three arguments instead of a value; not a
    // function or a state, so neither skip mechanism below can reach it, and
    // goal_src carries the same raw marker verbatim (this landing never compiled).
    // Same shape as gsound/joint/process-drawable above: whole file, not a function.
    "credits-obs",
    // title-obs: same class as credits-obs above, *end-credits-proc* is a raw
    // <static-data L226> blob in a top-level define; goal_src carries the same
    // raw marker verbatim. (Its five defstate handlers with raw-label-leak
    // :post/:code/:enter slots would each need their own skip_compile_states
    // entry too, but this file-level skip already makes those moot, so they are
    // not added.)
    "title-obs",
    // hud-static-literals rung: the decompiler emits two non-identical
    // internal-named (method hud-method-26 hang-time-hud-single) definitions
    // (COMMON and GAME DGO copies decode to different bytecode, the same
    // duplicate-object-file class as attackable-hash above) and goalc
    // refuses the duplicate; goal_src keeps the fuller of the two (the one
    // with the get-current-language text-id switch) and the decomp-vs-REF
    // diff still gates the rest of the object
    "hud-widgets-powerhang",
    // levels-other-tier rung: *race-state* is a raw <static-data L15> blob
    // like credits-obs/title-obs above, but its 272 raw words are all zero
    // (verified against the scoped ir2.asm), so unlike those two goal_src
    // does NOT carry the raw marker verbatim: it lands as
    // (new 'static 'race-state) with no field overrides, a faithful
    // transcription of an all-zero instance rather than an invented one, and
    // this DOES compile ((mi) Successfully built all 677 targets). The skip
    // is here only because the offline-test round-trip (compile this REF,
    // re-decompile, diff) can never match: the decompiler regenerates the
    // same unresolvable <static-data L15> form from the compiled output
    // every time, a decompiler limitation on large all-zero static blobs,
    // not a defect in the landing.
    "race-manager",
    // race-mesh rung (jakx-levels-other-tier-4): methods 13, 14, 17, 18 and
    // 19 all produce the decompiler's "expression building failed"
    // fallback, either no body at all (17, 18: "function has no type
    // analysis. Cannot decompile.") or bare (call!) pseudo-ops and
    // reserved-register locals (13, 14, 19: sp-0 typed and used as a plain
    // value), neither of which is valid GOAL to compile; goal_src omits
    // all five rather than landing broken bodies, and the decomp-vs-REF
    // diff still gates the seven methods that did land clean.
    "race-mesh",
    // race-line rung (jakx-levels-other-tier-4): the raw decode's own
    // reconstruction of test-find-line-info emits
    // (-> (+ (the-as uint v1-0) 112) query-position quad), chaining a field
    // access off a freshly-computed raw address; goalc looks up
    // query-position as a global rather than treating it as a field access
    // on that address and refuses to compile. goal_src casts the computed
    // address straight to vector ((-> (the-as vector (+ ...)) quad)),
    // exactly the same 128 bits query-position/quad would have reached, and
    // that does compile ((mi) Successfully built all N targets); the
    // decomp-vs-REF diff still gates the rest of the object.
    "race-line",
    // levels-other-tier rung: in-game-menu-hud needed a whole cluster of
    // hand touches goalc caught that the raw decode does not surface on its
    // own: the (defmethod hud-method-19/17/20/18 () (none)) blocks that
    // decoded this-less while hud's methods 17 to 21 were declared () none
    // (the hud remainder rung synced those to (_type_) none, and the
    // landing now carries the real receiver forms); five externs need real define-extern
    // declarations in this file for goalc to see them, decompiler-config
    // externs only guide the decompiler; nine duplicate deactivate methods
    // and three duplicate hud-method-22 methods (the "exists in multiple
    // non-identical object files" class, matching attackable-hash and
    // hud-widgets-powerhang above) need deduplication; and
    // spawn-hud-in-game-menu-networked's own raw decode never fully
    // resolved (expression building failed, leaving non-compilable .call!
    // pseudo-ops), hand-folded from the raw op evidence into real calls and
    // explicit pointer casts. goal_src carries all of this; (mi)
    // Successfully built all 649 targets; the decomp-vs-REF diff still
    // gates the whole object, which this skip only lifts the compile gate
    // for.
    "in-game-menu-hud",
    // wvehicle-weapons-h (vehicle band): two items omitted from goal_src rather
    // than landed raw. weapon-mask->type has no type at all (giving it a real
    // signature crashes the decompiler outright, "Assertion failed: 'is_var()'",
    // decompiler/IR2/AtomicOp.h:156, isolated with only this extern toggled;
    // see the commented-out extern's note in all-types.gc); *weapon-suppression-
    // table*'s own static (L34, 21 back-to-back separately-boxed (array symbol)
    // records) fails every label_types path tried and the decompiler emits an
    // unparseable <static-data L34> placeholder instead. Neither symbol has a
    // caller anywhere else in the corpus, so both are omitted entirely (the
    // credits-obs precedent) rather than carried as an uncompilable raw marker;
    // the decomp-vs-REF diff still gates the rest of the object.
    "wvehicle-weapons-h",
    // vehicle-debris (vehicle band): *vehicle-debris-constants* is a raw
    // <static-data L59> blob, a top-level define; not a function or a state,
    // so neither skip mechanism below can reach it, credits-obs precedent.
    // goal_src also omits methods 65, 87 and 88 (roughly 1,030 of this
    // file's 1,230 raw-decode lines, an almost entirely the-as-none
    // raw-offset fallback none of the three isolates cleanly out of) and the
    // two no-type-analysis functions vehicle-debris-init-by-other and
    // vehicle-debris-spawn. goal_src keeps the rest (both types, methods 3,
    // 66, 61, 80, 71, and the explode/fade-out/die state family); whole-file
    // skip is used rather than per-function entries because the omitted
    // symbol has no skip mechanism of its own.
    "vehicle-debris",
    // vehicle-manager (vehicle band): *car-info-default* is a raw
    // <static-data L78> blob, a top-level define with no skip mechanism of
    // its own (credits-obs precedent). goal_src also omits
    // vehicle-init-by-other, vehicle-in-level?, vehicle-spawn and
    // find-vehicle (an already-documented cross-band blocker needing
    // traffic-object-spawn-params, the race/vehicle band's own typing
    // territory) and vehicle-idx-from-level-name (a decompiler-side
    // dynamic-array-field-access gap). vehicle-manager-init-by-other and
    // vehicle-manager-start are also omitted (rigid-body-queue rung,
    // 2026-08-17): rigid-body-queue now lands its own deftype, spawn
    // wrapper and most methods, but rigid-body-queue-manager's own init-by-
    // other/idle-state/post cluster stays held there because method 10 (the
    // physics tick idle:post reaches on the first frame) diverges from
    // jak3's twin in ways that rung could not verify; landing vehicle-
    // manager-init-by-other here would activate that unverified chain via
    // rigid-body-queue-manager-spawn. See rigid-body-queue.gc's own held-
    // method notes. goal_src keeps the rest (the type, method 3, methods
    // 7/10/18/17, vehicle-manager-event-handler/-kill, the idle/active
    // states, and *car-appearance-hack*); whole-file skip is used rather
    // than per-function entries because the omitted symbol has none
    // available.
