    // supplies a real type to retype it from (its only caller,
    // hud-string-draw-all, is itself skipped below with no landed body).
    // Retyping arg0 without call-site evidence would be a guess, not a
    // derived signature; see hud.gc's own og:preserve-this note.
    "(method 9 hud-string)",
    // hud rung: hud-create-icon's fresh decode still fails type prop on
    // (l.wu (+ a0 192)) against the spawned manipy's ppointer-dereferenced
    // process, and separately fails to guess the static label use for L145
    // (its own manipy-init argument literal). No caller anywhere in this
    // corpus was found for it (grepped every _ir2.asm), so it is dead code
    // as far as this rung can tell. No landed body; its extern signature is
    // landed in decompiler/config/jakx/all-types.gc so a future caller
    // type-checks correctly.
    "hud-create-icon",
    // hud-effects rung: (method 14 hud-text-effect-sound) has a clean decode
    // but unconditionally dispatches net-game-mgr-method-45 and
    // game-text-info-method-10, neither landed anywhere in this corpus. No
    // landed body; hud-text-effect-sound inherits hud-effect's own landed
    // method-14 (net-hud.gc) in the meantime, the normal virtual-dispatch
    // behavior for an unfilled vtable slot, not a jump to zero.
    "(method 14 hud-text-effect-sound)",
    // hud-widgets-tier rung: (method 19 hud-headset-talker) has a clean decode
    // but its *headset* decoder-slot read is the addition-result cast class
    // documented as a wall in type_casts.jsonc; goalc rejects the decompiler's
